WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:05.960
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and no you aren’t
dreaming, Stephen Amell was spotted leaning

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:09.590
in for a Felicity Kiss in a new Arrow Season
3 Promo.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:13.490
I’ll explain what’s going on.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:18.460
But in response to the craziness I’m going
to do my top 5 superhero couples.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.180
Plus, some big news.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.480
Rila Fukushima is replacing Devin Aoki as
Katana.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.640
I’ll explain what happened there too.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.640
Important stuff first.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.300
If you were on twitter last night you may
have seen the hashtag Olicity Kiss flying

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.300
around.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.270
It was a little mysterious because the CW
hadn’t posted any official videos to social.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.280
But yet, there was a super short video of
Oliver almost kissing Felicity.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:51.710
When you zoom in what’s going on is he’s
leaning in and whispering something too her.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.740
If you remember the finale moment where “Slade
Took The Wrong Woman”?

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:00.989
It’s kind of like that, where oliver is
rather ambiguously showing affection and communicating

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:02.140
something secret.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:06.430
There’s no context for the scene so don’t
take it at face value.

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:10.380
The show does a great job of building the
Olicity sexual tension without trampling on

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.540
the future.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:18.250
In the spirit of that, here’s my top 5 Comic
Book Couples, these are from any verse, not

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.360
just Marvel and DC.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.170
Number 5 - Black Panther and Storm, Marvel’s
biggest Royal Couple

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:29.100
Bringing them together was a huge deal for
the fandom after the Civil War arc, but behind

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:35.370
the scenes it was also the big thing connecting
the X-Men franchise to the Avengers.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:36.930
Marvel’s two biggest teams.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:42.100
They were both born as royalty so it was also
like a comic book version of the royal wedding.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.210
Marvel has always had a lot of fun with epic
weddings.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:48.939
I think the wedding of Jean Grey in 1994 was
the next biggest thing in comics after the

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:51.979
Death of Superman arc and the Batman Knightfall
saga.

00:01:51.979 --> 00:01:55.310
Cyclops and Jean Grey were never my favorite
couple though.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:02:00.990
Recently things have not gone so hot, the
X-Men vs Avengers arc was basically the end

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:01.990
of their marriage.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.689
You can blame the Phoenix for that divorce.

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:06.510
Number 4 - Superman and Wonder Woman

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:16.349
This was such a big deal when they got together
in the New 52 comics.

00:02:16.349 --> 00:02:20.010
They’d already done the story in Kingdom
Come, but that was an alternate universe and

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.079
not considered canon of the mai versions of
the characters.

00:02:23.079 --> 00:02:31.760
New 52 was the DC reboot that established
a single continuity and Superman Wonder Woman

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.849
was one of the first big WTFs.

00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:37.559
You can let me know whether you love them
together or totally hate the idea.

00:02:37.559 --> 00:02:43.450
It’s like when Marvel rebooted Spider-Man
so that he wasn’t married to Mary Jane anymore.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:47.410
It’s hard to believe they didn’t let these
two A-Listers date before.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:52.569
Part of the attraction is that they’re both
alien gods so far on the fringe that they’re

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:55.219
pretty much undateable outside of a certain
tier.

00:02:55.219 --> 00:02:58.799
Like unless you are nearly indestructible,
you are not going to be able to have a sexual

00:02:58.799 --> 00:03:01.129
relationship with one of them or carry their
child.

00:03:01.129 --> 00:03:05.030
I remember when I read Kingdom Come for the
first time and saw Wonder Woman pregnant.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:08.459
All I could think about was what that baby’s
powers would be.

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:12.540
Their powers both appear similar but there’s
a lot of celestial magic tied to wonder woman’s

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.090
origin so theories below.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:17.750
What would their kid be like?

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.169
Number 3 - Green Arrow and Black Canary

00:03:19.169 --> 00:03:24.269
I know Arrow teased it a little, but since
they’re telling an origin story, there’s

00:03:24.269 --> 00:03:26.919
no way Oliver is going to get married in the
second season.

00:03:26.919 --> 00:03:30.159
In the comics it was a lot of fun.

00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:40.349
There interesting thing about them breaking
up in the comics was that it happened after

00:03:40.349 --> 00:03:48.139
Oliver killed Prometheus after Prometheus
killed Roy Harper’s daughter.

00:03:48.139 --> 00:03:49.420
That was just a string of tragedies.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:51.830
I’d be surprised if any marriage could survive
that.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:56.659
That was also just a terrible story for Roy,
somebody make sure Colton Haynes stays away

00:03:56.659 --> 00:03:57.659
from that.

00:03:57.659 --> 00:03:59.069
Reading it will just make him depressed.

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:01.451
Number 2 - Batman and Catwoman

00:04:01.451 --> 00:04:05.849
If you ever read the Earth 2 comics, the Huntress
was the daughter of Batman and the Selina

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:06.849
Kyle Catwoman.

00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:08.059
Her name was Helena Wayne.

00:04:08.059 --> 00:04:09.389
That was an alternate universe version.

00:04:09.389 --> 00:04:12.129
The version that Arrow did was Helena Bertinelli.

00:04:12.129 --> 00:04:18.260
They never got married in the main comics,
but they had sex so many times you’d think

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:19.709
they were living together.

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:26.040
Rule #1 of Batman relationships is that nothing
lasts forever, even with a Lazarus Pit.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:30.000
They did get together in the new 52 comics,
but their relationship is described as being

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.410
estranged.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:35.220
Which basically means you broke up but you
still booty call each other with the bat signal

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.220
on occasion.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:40.850
I’m interested to see what kind of a relationship
the Gotham tv show is going to give the bruce

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:43.590
wayne and catwoman characters since they’re
only little kids.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.620
I’m guessing they’ll just become good
friends that help each other out.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:47.620
Just for reference, I think Bruce Wayne is
supposed to be about 13 on the show.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.460
and my Number 1 Comic Book couple - Gambit
and Rogue

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:53.360
The thing that really made me love the two
of them together was the 90s cartoon.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:56.820
I watched that more than I read the comics.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:01.530
The fun thing about the two of them was that
they were always a pair of loveable scoundrels.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:05.370
They weren’t royalty like Storm and Black
Panther, so the seemed more like people you

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:06.530
would want to hang out with.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.870
That’s the problem with a lot of the A-List
mega superheroes.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:12.710
It’s almost like the more powerful you get
the more uptight you get.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:18.280
Gambit and Rogue were the couple that made
you forget about Apocalypse and Magneto.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:23.210
Lately the comics haven’t been so nice to
them.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:31.260
Gambit became one of Apocalypse’s four horsemen
but in his spinoff comic they have teased

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.260
a reconcilliation.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:35.540
Rule Number 1 of any comic book couple: Nothing
lasts forever.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:39.350
But rule number 2 is everything comes back
around eventually.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:42.260
So even if people break up, they’ll probably
get back together at some point.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:46.110
There’s always something bad about getting
everything you want.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:52.030
In the life of a comic book superhero, nothing
is permanent.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:56.140
So the minute you have everything, something
jumps out to stab you in the back.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:58.000
A villain returns, like Malcolm Merlyn.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.831
Just to tie it back to Arrow.

00:05:59.831 --> 00:06:01.720
You get distracted and new threats develop,
like Count Vertigo and your girlfriends face

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:06.430
shines so brightly that you can’t see the
shadows moving in the distance.

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:10.380
Shadows in this case being the League of Assassins
and Ra’s Al Ghul.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:20.070
As a fan of the characters, that’s the big
reason I don’t want the show to completely

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:21.190
go there.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:26.110
Oliver and Felicity will always be a family
with the rest of Team Arrow, but only in the

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.730
sense you deeply care about each other.

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:31.350
Let me know if you agree, but I feel like
it’s an unspoken rule that the biggest superheroes

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:34.230
and supervillains don’t get to have traditional
happy families.

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:38.000
They can have children, but they can’t have
normal relationships.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.940
Batman has Talia and Damien, but that doesn’t
end well at all.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:44.780
Oliver in the comics has Connor and they have
a terrible relationship.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:46.090
Here’s a big question for you guys.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.670
If Oliver and Felicity ever really did get
together, do you think it would kill the dynamic

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:50.670
in the group.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:54.640
The minute he started having sex with black
canary everything went south.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:58.389
There’s no wrong answer, but I feel like
not knowing how they’ll end up is more exciting

00:06:58.389 --> 00:07:02.970
than seeing it at the risk of being disappointed
after.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:09.000
On to Katana, the big news is that Devin Aoki
has been replaced by Rila Fukushima because

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.070
of scheduling conflicts.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:14.860
When they say scheduling conflicts, usually
what happens is actors get signed to a contract

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:18.560
for a specific period of time when the show
expects to be filming their scenes.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.041
Shooting days get moved around all the time,
so it’s likely that Devin Aoki’s shooting

00:07:20.041 --> 00:07:22.940
schedule for Arrow changed and overlapped
with some other movie she was doing or vis

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:23.940
versa.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.940
Arrow was probably getting ready to film some
Katana scenes and needed an actress, so they

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:26.940
find a new Katana.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:28.860
It just so happens that their new actress
was also Yukio in the last Wolverine movie.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.270
One step closer to a Marvel DC crossover.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:34.630
I did a big video explaining Katana’s backstory
in the comics that I’ll link in the description.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:42.650
But the idea is that the show will use her
in the Hong Kong flashbacks and in the present.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:45.670
Usually when characters from the flashbacks
come forward it’s because they’re tied

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:48.720
up in the big villain arc.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:54.710
Like Black Canary and Slade in season 2.

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:58.650
This season Ra’s Al Ghul is the big bad,
so if Katana is going to show up in the past

00:07:58.650 --> 00:07:59.830
and the present.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.990
It probably has something to do with him and
the League of Assassins.

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:07.190
That makes me wonder if The League of Assassins
has something to do with Amanda Waller’s

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:08.440
Hong Kong operation.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:12.330
They do a good job of putting clues about
the big villain arc in the season premiere

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:17.130
every year so make sure to keep your eyes
peeled for things that connect Katana, Oliver,

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:20.270
Amanda Waller and Ra’s Al Ghul.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:24.550
Fukushima is a great action actress so she
will be a total badass on Arrow.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:29.760
Speaking of crossover characters, there’s
another Tommy Flashback scene in Hong Kong.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:33.719
Supposedly Tommy is there for some unrelated
reason and Oliver almost runs into him.

00:08:33.719 --> 00:08:39.219
Which makes me wonder if Malcolm Merlyn will
show in the flashbacks too.

00:08:39.219 --> 00:08:50.180
He was back in starling city while oliver
was away for that 5 year period.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:53.600
Merlyn’s time with the league of assassins
preceded Oliver’s shipwreck.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:56.769
So far he hasn’t been in any of the promos
yet.

00:08:56.769 --> 00:09:06.800
They should be releasing the now infamous
Olicity Kiss one, so maybe they’ll expand

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:09.189
that and add some Merlyn.

00:09:09.189 --> 00:09:19.160
I’m not expecting to see any of the other
guest comic book characters in promos, other

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.529
than Ray Palmer.

00:09:21.529 --> 00:09:38.440
They’ll probably release some more footage
of him to explain his character a little better.

